<item><title>Ethiopia’s startup law opens incentives to foreign founders</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/et/ethiopia-s-startup-law-opens-incentives-to-foreign-founders-f1512e/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/et/ethiopia-s-startup-law-opens-incentives-to-foreign-founders-f1512e/</guid><category>Ethiopia</category><description>Article 40 allows foreign startups and ecosystem builders to access incentives, while excluding foreign startups from the grant programme.</description><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:00:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/et.jpg" length="32890" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/et.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Ethiopian-born children report unequal access to citizenship</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/et/ethiopian-born-children-report-unequal-access-to-citizenship-4bea60/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/et/ethiopian-born-children-report-unequal-access-to-citizenship-4bea60/</guid><category>Ethiopia</category><description>Some children of Ethiopian mothers and foreign fathers say they struggle to secure nationality, while another man obtained an identity card and passport without difficulty.</description><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:00:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/et.jpg" length="32890" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/et.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Ethiopia&apos;s ride-hailing sector pays 340 million birr in income tax</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/et/ethiopia-s-ride-hailing-sector-pays-340-million-birr-in-37b937/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/et/ethiopia-s-ride-hailing-sector-pays-340-million-birr-in-37b937/</guid><category>Ethiopia</category><description>More than 30 platforms compete in Addis Ababa on fares and vehicle types, while 33,000 drivers, most of them self-employed, carry the costs of fuel and rent.</description><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:00:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/et/ethiopia-s-ride-hailing-sector-pays-340-million-birr-in-37b937/share.jpg" length="42389" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/et/ethiopia-s-ride-hailing-sector-pays-340-million-birr-in-37b937/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Exporters warn smuggling is undermining Ethiopia’s pulses and oilseeds trade</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/et/exporters-warn-smuggling-is-undermining-ethiopia-s-pulses-7f9a36/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/et/exporters-warn-smuggling-is-undermining-ethiopia-s-pulses-7f9a36/</guid><category>Ethiopia</category><description>The exporters’ association says illegal channels are weakening formal sales as Ethiopia seeks to expand processing, quality and overseas markets.</description><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:00:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/et.jpg" length="32890" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/et.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
